{
  "_README": [
    "What a room is for, and what that means it holds. Authored by hand — unlike prop_catalog.json,",
    "nothing here is derived from the packs.",
    "",
    "A purpose is eligible for a room when its area and storey constraints pass; among eligible",
    "rooms it prefers the ones its wants* fields score highest. Each want is -1..1 and reads",
    "against the map's own spread: wantsArea 1 means 'the biggest rooms on this map', wantsDepth 1",
    "means 'as far from the entrance as this map goes', wantsDegree -1 means 'a dead end'.",
    "weight only decides the filler draw once quotas are served, and is damped each time the",
    "purpose is used so one purpose cannot take a whole dungeon.",
    "",
    "minArea/maxArea are plausibility bounds, not the selector — the wants do the selecting, and",
    "they are relative to the map, so they keep working whatever the sizes are. Room areas differ",
    "by size preset far more than is obvious (median 100 on small, 154 on medium, 216 on large), so",
    "an absolute cap tuned by eye against a small map quietly excludes a purpose from large ones",
    "altogether: maxArea 90 on Cell left 4% of large-map rooms eligible and a quota of two cells",
    "could not be met. Keep every band above roughly one room in six on all three presets, and",
    "re-measure rather than reason about it if Padding or RoomFill ever change.",
    "",
    "zones name prop groups from prop_catalog.json, which are the pack authors' own GroupTags:",
    "  wall   — backed against a wall, facing into the room",
    "  corner — tucked into an interior corner, turned into the angle",
    "  centre — standing clear of the walls",
    "A group that resolves to nothing is skipped silently, so naming an absent one costs only the",
    "variety it would have added. `MapGenQA recipes` prints what each zone actually resolves to.",
    "",
    "light is per style rather than per purpose: every furnished room gets lit, at a fixed spacing",
    "along its walls, whatever it is for."
  ],

